\paragraph{The inferential unit, and why the trial counts are not the sample size.} Table~\ref{tab:sample_sizes} above counts \emph{trials}. For the criterion-4 evidence---the only place this paper reports a positive---trials are \textbf{nested}, and the unit that carries the inference is the \textbf{paired claim} within a target, not the trial. Table~\ref{tab:inference_ladder} states the nesting explicitly, because the trial totals are three orders of magnitude larger than the level at which the claim is actually made.

